<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phillippe de Longvilliers de Poincy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1584">1584</a>–<a href="/years/1660">1660</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Philippe de Longvilliers de Poincy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phillippe de Longvilliers de Poincy was a Knight Hospitaller who became governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-antilles">French Antilles</a> from 1639, ruling from Saint Christophe. He defied the French company and crown, and in 1651 persuaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Order of Saint John</a> to buy Saint Christophe, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-barthelemy">Saint Barthélemy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-martin-island">Saint Martin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-croix">Saint Croix</a>, which he governed for the knights until his death.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>French settlers from Saint Kitts, sent by the governor <b>Philippe de Longvilliers de Poincy</b>, occupied Saint-Barthélemy in 1648.</blockquote><a href="/state/french-saint-barthelemy">French Saint-Barthélemy</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Philippe de Longvilliers de Poincy</b>, governor-general of the French Antilles from 1639, ruled from a grand château on the island and bought it for the Knights of Malta in 1651.</blockquote><a href="/state/french-saint-christophe">French Saint-Christophe</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1650 forces sent by <b>Philippe de Longvilliers de Poincy</b>, governor of the French Antilles, expelled the Spanish and occupied the island.</blockquote><a href="/state/french-saint-croix">French Saint Croix</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Philippe de Longvilliers de Poincy</b>, a Knight of Malta and governor-general of the French Antilles, persuaded the order to buy the French shares of Saint Kitts, Saint Martin, Saint-Barthélemy and Saint Croix from the bankrupt Compagnie des Îles d'Amérique.</blockquote><a href="/state/hospitaller-caribbean-colonies">Hospitaller Caribbean colonies</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Kitts</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=17.32,-62.75&amp;year=1633" aria-label="Saint Kitts on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2845 1521 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Phillippe de Longvilliers de Poincy"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3295 1791h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3295 1791h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=17.32,-62.75&amp;year=1633">What was here in 1633? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
